# Status-basis invariant

**Invariant:** `∀ status s crossing a boundary: s = {value, as_of, source, scope, epoch}` — **no bare boolean
crosses a boundary.** A consumer given `{ok: true}` cannot tell an `rc` from a delivery receipt; given
`exposure_mismatch: true` cannot tell mark notional from entry notional; given `TAB_READY` cannot tell which
epoch. Validity is the time-axis slice of this; observable, scope and units are the others.

Boundary = process, agent-bus turn, HTTP payload, file on disk, MCP tool response. Doctrine:
`decision:status-basis-invariant`. Evidence: agent-bus:99998 turns 6–7 (six instances, two classes).

## Four axes — a status is judgeable only when all four are present

| Axis | Field | Failure when absent (observed instance) |
|---|---|---|
| **Observable** | `source` — *what* was measured (rc, DOM receipt, WS cache, REST, ledger sum) | uinput `rc=0` reported as `ok=True` delivery; paste landed in Chrome (10462#33) |
| **Scope** | `scope` — over *which* input set (lane vs returned window, per-row vs aggregate) | `tab_ready` true at `last=10`, false at `last=3`, same lane, same minute |
| **Units** | operands + units carried with any comparison | `exposure_mismatch = |mark_notional − fill_notional| > 1.0` flip-flopping on ticks |
| **Epoch / as_of** | `as_of` timestamp + `epoch` (the event that invalidates) | dead-tab `TAB_READY` passing the gate; `GO` surviving a manual flatten (9740#88) |

## Rules

- **Emit:** a status object, never a bool. Comparisons carry both operands and their units
  (`{a, a_unit, b, b_unit, tolerance, as_of}`), not the verdict alone.
- **Consume:** validity is **derived by the consumer that acts**, from `(epoch event, TTL, verified_at)` — never
  read from a stored flag. Stored booleans drift by construction (class B); scratchboards are stored flags.
- **Unskippable:** place the derivation at the single chokepoint that performs the effect (the order-placing
  function, the paste-performing function), not at each caller. A convention-side check fails open the moment a
  second path appears (`intent.expires_at` checked in `ems.py`, skipped by `fire.py`).
- **TTL needs refresh:** any TTL without an activity-refresh rule lies in the other direction
  (`tab_ready_stale` refusing a tab that had just answered, 10462#37). Same-seat activity refreshes.
- **TTL names its observable and the stream semantics.** Age of the last frame on a push-on-change
  (replace-on-update) stream is *time since last change*, not staleness — a TTL on it is a false-stale
  generator (Lighter account WS: idle gaps p99 ~57 min; a 300 s gate on `age_s` refuses every idle hour).
  Bound periodic observables (`rest_verified_at`, heartbeat) instead, or the stream's own stall backstop.
- **A summary boolean over a measurable quantity is legitimate when it publishes the predicate it
  summarises** — `{value, scope, threshold, reason}` — and illegitimate otherwise. `degraded: false` with
  `scope: account_ws_idle, stall_backstop_s: 7200, reason: ws_connected_idle_within_backstop` is readable from
  the object; bare `degraded: false` is `ok: true` again.
- **Success-shaped ≠ success:** read the response's own fields before claiming an effect
  (`sidecar_uri: null` on HTTP 200; `notify` 200 with `status: disabled`). Pairs with `provenance-discipline`.
- **Fail closed on degrade:** when a producer cannot deliver the content its shape promises, return an error
  naming what is required, or partial content plus an explicit overflow pointer — never a 200-shaped envelope
  (index, stub, empty codec) a caller can consume as content.

## Worked instances — the check exists and one path skips it

| Surface | Contract present | Path that skipped it | Lesson |
|---|---|---|---|
| Trader fire path | `intent.expires_at` (`trader/intent.py:326`), checked in `ems.py:83–90` | `fire.py fire_intent` relays without consulting it | Consumer-side convention fails open on the second path; the check belongs at the order-placing chokepoint (`POST /commands/enter-symbol` → `enter_symbol()`) |
| Continuity tape pour | response carried `truncated=true`, `payload_bytes=76230 > budget_bytes=30000`, `codec_counts.messages-v1=0` | consumer read the 350-entry index as content | Basis was present; the consumer did not read it. Producer must fail closed (error or partial+overflow URI) instead of a truncated success |
| perps `data_freshness.degraded` | 7200 s silent-stall backstop on the account WS (`ws_live_view.py`) | reader saw `degraded: false, age_s: 2889` and inferred a threshold the field never published; a downstream gate applied its own 300 s TTL to the same `age_s` | The boolean was true to its predicate; the object did not carry the predicate. Fix is the invariant applied literally: publish `scope` + `stall_backstop_s`, `reason` never null |

Two independent surfaces, one shape: a contract that exists and is consulted by convention is not a contract.
- **Genus:** an append-only event ledger is not a continuity root; current state is derived from the authoritative
  source (venue, filesystem, registry) at read, never from the ledger's newest row.

- **A computed value replaced by a floor or default must publish that it was replaced, and what the computed
  value was.** `max(computed, floor)` returning the floor silently is the general shape; a field named
  `effective_*` that is sometimes computed and sometimes a constant, with no way to tell which, is the
  reader-facing half (`compute_position_size` → Kelly says bet 0 on a −EV strategy, `max(0, MIN_SIZE_USDC)`
  serves `effective_size_usdc: 40.0`; the only instance that costs money continuously rather than at an incident).
- **A persistence layer whose tests can write the production path is a class of its own.** The first run of
  the durable-halt test wrote `{halts: {}}` over the live `data/risk_halts.json` — the safety mechanism would
  have disarmed itself at the moment it existed to fire. Every persisted-state module ships with an autouse
  fixture that pins its path to `tmp_path`; a status file the tests can reach is not durable state.

## Anti-patterns

`{ok: True}` from an exit code · a bool computed over a paginated window · a `$` tolerance between quantities in
different units · a readiness token with no epoch · a `role:root` tag on a machine-written ledger · fixing one
consumer path and calling the class closed.
